        "math_academy_id": "q-102807",
        "knowledge_point_id": "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952",
        "knowledge_point": "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization",
        "problem": "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2y=x+3 \\\\ 7-y=-x\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-x+2y=3 \\\\ x-y=-7.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
